      "status": "unresolved_semantics",
      "resolution": "The escalation that reads the counter: alptramun_summon.lua summons 1-4 dreams (up to 5 summons, as Alptramun's summons) whose type rises with AlptramunSummonsKilled in bands of nine. No Canary monster casts this spell (it is not in Alptramun's attacks or defenses), and summoned dreams have a master, so this script would not count them. The reference-date wiki says Alptramun \"will initially appear with several summons. These summons, when killed, will be replaced by even stronger summons\" without numbers; defining that ability (an ability_cast rule, D29) needs its exact rule from the owner or further evidence."
